# Service account keys. Never commit these — anyone with the file can bill
# your Google Cloud project. The broad patterns are deliberate: real key
# filenames look like <project>-<16 hex chars>.json and would slip past a
# narrower rule.
service-account-key.json
*.key.json
*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]*.json
**/ee-backend/
venv/

# Benchmark / ingest scratch output
/tmp-cogs/

# Generated into the Vite build by vercel.json buildCommand
web/public/demo.html
verify-report.md

# Agent skills installed by `npx skills add`.
#
# Vendored tooling, not project code — ~300 files that have nothing to do with
# Site Scanner and would show up in every diff and every clone. skills-lock.json
# IS tracked, so `npx skills install` reproduces the exact same set: the lockfile
# is the record, the payload is not.
.agents/skills/
.claude/skills/
